.TH CIXCAT 1 "CIX 0.1.0" "CIX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cixcat \- restore a CIX archive to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cixcat
.RI [ archive ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cixcat
is the streaming-output form of
.BR uncix .
It restores ARCHIVE, or standard input when ARCHIVE is omitted or
.BR \- ,
to standard output. It is intended for pipelines.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.EX
cixcat backup.tar.cix | tar -x
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the CIX version and supported container identifiers.
.SH RESOURCE LIMITS
The decoder starts with a 6 GiB accounted working-memory admission limit unless an explicit limit is supplied. This
is not an aggregate-process RSS guarantee; apply normal operating-system process limits when using CIX in an automated pipeline.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. A nonzero status indicates invalid input, an integrity
failure, I/O failure, resource admission failure, or interruption.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cix (1),
.BR uncix (1)
